# Line endings, so a fresh clone passes `npm run check`. Card #0074.
#
# **Without this file the gate fails on every TypeScript file after a clone.** Git stores
# LF in the index, `core.autocrlf=true` converts to CRLF on checkout, and Biome's
# formatter wants LF. Nobody had noticed because this repository had only ever been
# cloned onto one machine, and every file on disk here was written by an editor rather
# than by a checkout.
#
# **Found 2026-08-19 by accident.** A `git checkout -- src/routes/device.ts` during an
# unrelated revert brought that one file back as CRLF. `git ls-files --eol` then read
# `i/lf w/crlf` for it and `i/lf w/lf` for all 57 of its neighbors, and Biome failed on
# exactly the file git had touched.
#
# **`eol=lf` makes checkout write LF whatever anyone's `core.autocrlf` says**, which is
# what the gate already expects. It changes no history and produces no diff today,
# because the index is already LF -- it changes what a FUTURE checkout writes.
*       text=auto eol=lf

# **Binaries MUST be exempt, or `text=auto` corrupts them.** Git's heuristic is good and
# it is a heuristic; naming the formats this repository actually carries costs one line
# and removes the guess. A mangled font or screenshot fails in a way nobody traces back
# to a line-ending rule.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
